            <text x="390" y="192" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Inter,sans-serif" font-size="9.5" fill="rgba(240,236,226,0.8)" text-decoration="underline" style="cursor:pointer;">AI-Powered UX Design</text>
            <text x="390" y="203" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Inter,sans-serif" font-size="7.5" fill="rgba(255,255,255,0.3)" font-style="italic">tap for more</text>
          </g>
          <g class="venn-circle-group" pointer-events="all" onclick="showOverlapInfo('hci-info','Security Usability','Where HCI and Cybersecurity meet: security that is not usable is not secure. If users cannot understand a security warning, they will dismiss it. If authentication is too complex, they will find workarounds. If consent language is inaccessible, they cannot make informed decisions. Human-centered design is not in tension with cybersecurity; it is the mechanism through which cybersecurity actually works for real people.')">
