          <div class="venn-card-title" style="color:rgba(45,210,180,0.95);">Society &amp; General Population</div>
          <div class="venn-card-body">Everyone using AI-powered technology daily, banking, healthcare, social media, government services, multimedia platforms, workplace automation, entertainment, is living at this intersection, whether they know it or not. Every time a person encounters an AI-powered system, three things are happening simultaneously: they are navigating an interface shaped by HCI principles, making decisions with security consequences, and engaging with technology that is learning from them. Trust at a societal level is formed and eroded through these individual interactions. When systems are designed without the full range of human experience in mind, society as a whole bears the cost. Understanding this intersection is not a specialist concern. It is a civic one, and this research speaks to it as such.</div>
